  "question": {
    "text": "A Carnot engine with efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> takes heat from a source at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. In order to increase the efficiency to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, keeping the temperature of sink same, the new temperature of the source will be:",
    "image": null
